+Each framework's own tags become the report's tags ([Report Data Formats](Report-Data-Formats#tags)), a
+feature's and a scenario's apart:
+
+| Module | Feature tags | Scenario tags |
+|---|---|---|
+| `kronikol4j-junit5` | the class's `@Tag`s, with those JUnit gives it from its superclasses, interfaces and enclosing classes | the test method's own `@Tag`s |
+| `kronikol4j-testng` | the groups of the class-level `@Test` (the nearest one up the superclasses) | the method `@Test`'s groups |
+| `kronikol4j-spock` | the spec's `@Tag`s, then its super specs' | the feature method's `@Tag`s |
+| `kronikol4j-cucumber` | the `Feature:` line's tags | the pickle's tags: the scenario's, its rule's and its Examples block's |
+
+A scenario does not repeat a tag its feature carries. `endpoint:x` is the feature's endpoint and not a
+tag. `happy-path` on a test, a Gherkin scenario or an Examples block marks it the happy path; on a class,
+a spec, a feature file or a rule it marks no scenario.
+
